    <node id="Scheme::Stamp duty exemption on mortgaged and pledged documents">
      <data key="d0">Scheme</data>
      <data key="d1">Stamp duty exemption on mortgaged and pledged documents</data>
      <data key="d2">https://www.tn.gov.in/scheme_details.php?id=OA==</data>
      <data key="d3">Quantum of incentives-100%</data>
      <data key="d4">Any where in the state</data>
      <data key="d5" />
      <data key="d6">1.For issue of Eligibility Certificate (EC)
Within three months from the date of commencement of production or date of power connection,whichever is later.
2. For submission of subsidy claims
The first claim should be preferred within 30 days from the date of issue of EC.Subsequent claims should be submitted
once in six months i.e. the bills raised by Tamil Nadu Generation and Distribution Corporation Limited from January to June should be preferred before August 31st of the year and from July to December  before 28th of February of the succeeding year.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ApplicationMethod::1.For issue of Eligibility Certificate (EC)&#10;Within three months from the date of commencement of production or date of power connection,whichever is later.&#10;2. For submission of subsidy claims&#10;The first claim should be preferred within 30 days from the date of issue of EC.Subsequent claims should be submitted&#10;once in six months i.e. the bills raised by Tamil Nadu Generation and Distribution Corporation Limited from January to June should be preferred before August 31st of the year and from July to December  before 28th of February of the succeeding year.">
      <data key="d0">ApplicationMethod</data>
      <data key="d1">1.For issue of Eligibility Certificate (EC)
Within three months from the date of commencement of production or date of power connection,whichever is later.
2. For submission of subsidy claims
The first claim should be preferred within 30 days from the date of issue of EC.Subsequent claims should be submitted
once in six months i.e. the bills raised by Tamil Nadu Generation and Distribution Corporation Limited from January to June should be preferred before August 31st of the year and from July to December  before 28th of February of the succeeding year.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Scheme::Distribution of Gypsum - Oil Seeds">
      <data key="d0">Scheme</data>
      <data key="d1">Distribution of Gypsum - Oil Seeds</data>
      <data key="d2">https://www.tn.gov.in/scheme_details.php?id=MTU0NA==</data>
      <data key="d3">50% of the cost of material plus transport limited to Rs. 750/- per ha whichever is less.</data>
      <data key="d4">Those farmers who produce and supply Foundation and Certified Class seeds to the Department are elligible to avail of the benefit</data>
      <data key="d5" />
      <data key="d6">Application is to be submitted to:
Assistant Agricultural officer at the Village Level
Agricultural Officer / Deputy Agricultural Officer at the Block Level
The Assistant Director of Agriculture at the Block Level
The Joint Director of Agriculture at the District Level</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Scheme::Production of Certified  Seeds of Maize">
      <data key="d0">Scheme</data>
      <data key="d1">Production of Certified  Seeds of Maize</data>
      <data key="d2">https://www.tn.gov.in/scheme_details.php?id=OTAw</data>
      <data key="d3">Rs.1000/- per Quintal</data>
      <data key="d4">All maize growing farmers are eligible to avail of the subsidy under this scheme
in the Districts of Coimbatore, Dindigul, Erode, Dharmapuri, Krishnagiri, Namakkal,
Perambalur, Virudhunagar, Theni, Villupuram, Vellore, Salem, Pudukkottai, Madurai, Sivagangai, Trichy, Tirunelveli and Thoothukudi.
Preference will be given to Small/Marginal farmers
24% flow to SC/ST farmers will be ensured
20% flow to women farmers/ women groups</data>
      <data key="d5" />
      <data key="d6">The application is to be submitted to:
Assistant Agricultural officer at the Village Level
Agricultural Officer / Deputy Agricultural Officer at the Block Level
The Assistant Director of Agriculture at the Block Level
The Joint Director of Agriculture at the District Level</data>
    </node>
